From: mscharged-port
Subject: D3D12 resolves only what EFB passes draw
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance. Apply after 0129.

0124 limits the render area of multisampled EFB passes on Vulkan, the only
Dawn backend with RenderPassRenderAreaRect. D3D12 has Dawn's partial resolve
instead (DawnPartialLoadResolveTexture, RenderPassDescriptorResolveRect): such
a pass now resolves only the bounding box of its draws' scissors. Loads,
stores and draws stay as they are. Dawn resolves the rectangle with the render
pass's own resolve parameters, or with ResolveSubresourceRegion where it
emulates render passes (instead of ResolveSubresource for the whole texture).
Metal gets the render area from Dawn patch 0007.

